=== dataflow-bind-both-sides-of-equality.watsup ===
error[algo/bind-both-sides-of-equality]: both sides of an equality bind new variables: left side binds variable `x`, right side binds variable `y`
  --> dataflow-bind-both-sides-of-equality.watsup:14:9
   |
14 |   -- if x = y
   |         ^^^^^
   |
   | note: An `=` premise reads as a comparison when both sides are already
   |       bound, or as a binder when one side is. With new variables on both
   |       sides it fits neither.
=== dataflow-bind-in-non-invertible.watsup ===
error[algo/non-invertible-binding]: non-invertible unary operator contains newly bound variable `x`
  --> dataflow-bind-in-non-invertible.watsup:13:10
   |
13 |   -- if -x = 5
   |          ^
   |
   | note: Each variable in a binding expression must correspond directly to a
   |       tuple element, variant case argument, struct field, or list element.
   |       Operators are not inverted, even when their inverse would be unique.
=== dataflow-free-variable-in-output.watsup ===
error[algo/free-variable-in-expression]: expression uses unbound variable `u`
  --> dataflow-free-variable-in-output.watsup:14:8
   |
14 |   v |- u
   |        ^
   |
   | note: Every variable here must already be bound by an earlier part of the
   |       rule, such as the conclusion's input position or a preceding premise.
=== dataflow-iter-binding-only.watsup ===
error[algo/iteration-missing-loop-variable]: iteration has no loop variable because `x` is newly bound
  --> dataflow-iter-binding-only.watsup:13:7
   |
13 |   -- (if x = 0)*
   |       ^^^^^^^^
   |
   | note: An iteration needs a variable bound outside it whose values it can
   |       iterate over.
=== dataflow-parallel-binding-dimension-mismatch.watsup ===
error[algo/parallel-binding-dimension-mismatch]: parallel bindings for `x` have incompatible dimensions: `foo` and `foo*`
  --> dataflow-parallel-binding-dimension-mismatch.watsup:10:8
   |
10 |   (x, (x, y)*) |- true
   |        ^
   |
